Aging Calculation

Work order age is calculated based on the Work Order Received Date.
30 days from day WO was created
Calculation should be stored in a new field "Due Date"
The “Target Start Date” from the PDF is not used in aging calculations.
Aging is calculated in calendar days.
No exceptions for holidays or weekends
Aging updates automatically as time progresses without manual updates.
Visual Indicators

When a work order reaches 21 days, a warning icon is displayed.
When a work order reaches 30 days or more, a bold red critical icon is displayed.
The 21‑day and 30‑day icons are visually distinct.
Icons appear in all relevant work order list views. - TBD
Icons do not affect text readability, column layout, or row background colors.
View Readability

Icons are used instead of color‑coded rows or fields.
No new required fields (such as “Completion By” or “Due Date”) are introduced to support this feature.
Existing work order views do not require restructuring.
Scheduling Considerations

The solution supports future enhancement to introduce a Due Date / Completion By field.
If implemented, the Schedule Board can be ordered by Due Date.
Ordering the Schedule Board by Due Date is sufficient without requiring color or icon indicators.
